{
  "id": 222692716,
  "iid": 10548,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "rpm: don't overwrite user changes to diameter/Custom.xml on package upgrades",
  "description": "At least as part of RPM packages on Linux, Wireshark provides a file /usr/share/wireshark/diameter/Custom.xml. The \"custom\" part of the name implies this is the user-customizable part. As Diameter dictionaries don't seem to be supported within a user directory (unlike other parts of the configuration) out of the box, using a single system-wide customizable file makes sense. However, this file is not considered a user-modifiable configuration and is overwritten on every package upgrade. This MR fixes that.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2023-05-10T11:59:13.298Z",
  "updated_at": "2023-05-25T17:01:25.011Z",
